invariant: INV-26
file: aes_extern.c
catches: quic_test_extern
reason: aes_expand_round_keys zeros one byte past the eleven round keys
  aes_block.h says it writes. The schedule a caller holds is exactly
  that long in a build without AES-256, so the store lands on whatever
  the caller keeps next to it. bin/quic_test_extern marks the byte after
  the bound and requires it unchanged.

--- old
    memset(&round_keys[AES_128_KEY], 0, ((size_t)AES_ROUND_KEYS * AES_BLOCK) - AES_128_KEY);
--- new
    memset(&round_keys[AES_128_KEY], 0, ((size_t)AES_ROUND_KEYS * AES_BLOCK) - AES_128_KEY + 1);
